{%- comment -%}
  strict2-safe object lookup: the old dynamic form "[baType].title" (bare
  bracket access) is rejected by Shopify's strict2 Liquid validation, which
  made the whole snippet unsaveable on strict2 themes. Map the drop
  explicitly instead; unknown/blank baType falls back to shop, matching the
  old dynamic lookup's nil-for-missing-property behavior.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- case baType -%}
  {%- when 'product' -%}{%- assign booster_item = product -%}
  {%- when 'collection' -%}{%- assign booster_item = collection -%}
  {%- when 'article' -%}{%- assign booster_item = article -%}
  {%- when 'page' -%}{%- assign booster_item = page -%}
  {%- when 'blog' -%}{%- assign booster_item = blog -%}
  {%- else -%}{%- assign booster_item = shop -%}
{%- endcase -%}

{%- comment -%}
  "Use Shopify defaults" mode: when the merchant has selected this option for
  meta title or meta description, override whatever was assigned above with
  the [shopify_seo_title] / [shopify_seo_description] placeholders. The
  replacement step further down resolves these to Shopify's `page_title` and
  `page_description` Liquid variables, which mirror the merchant's native
  Shopify SEO fields. Single insertion point so all template types (product,
  collection, article, page, etc.) get consistent behavior, and so the
  storefront reflects the new mode immediately even before the next BatchScan.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if booster_config.auto_meta_title_active and booster_config.auto_meta_title_rules == 'shopify_seo_fields' -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = "[shopify_seo_title]" -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if booster_config.auto_meta_desc_active and booster_config.auto_meta_desc_rules == 'shopify_seo_fields' -%}
  {%- assign booster_desc = "[shopify_seo_description]" -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Multi-market safety net. On a NON-primary storefront locale, Booster must not
  replace the theme's native (Translate & Adapt) SEO title/description with its
  own single-language value -- doing so overwrites the merchant's translation
  (the exact bug multilingual stores hit). We detect the shop's primary locale
  and whether the current request is on a secondary market; the title and
  description blocks below then defer to page_title / page_description there, so
  Shopify's native per-locale translation is served untouched. The primary
  market keeps Booster's optimized meta. Per-shop opt-out via the
  disable_native_meta_fallback config flag (absent/false = feature on).
  strict2-safe: only standard loops/filters, no bracketed dynamic lookups.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ba_secondary_market = false -%}
{%- unless booster_config.disable_native_meta_fallback -%}
  {%- assign ba_primary_locale = '' -%}
  {%- for ba_loc in shop.published_locales -%}
    {%- if ba_loc.primary -%}{%- assign ba_primary_locale = ba_loc.iso_code -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if ba_primary_locale != '' and request.locale.iso_code != ba_primary_locale -%}
    {%- assign ba_secondary_market = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endunless -%}

{%- comment -%}booster:title:start{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Booster's snippet is injected first in <head>, so the <title> it emits is the
  one Google uses. When meta optimization is ON (booster_title present) we ALWAYS
  emit our optimized title: gating it would throw away the optimization the
  merchant pays for and let the theme's title win, a regression. We gate ONLY the
  non-optimized emissions (secondary-market passthrough and the meta-off
  page_title fallback), which merely echo the theme's own title and would
  otherwise add a redundant duplicate. booster_config.theme_has_native_title is
  set server-side from a stable homepage check; absent/false means "emit as
  before". A residual duplicate under meta-ON is resolved by removing the THEME's
  tag, not ours.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if ba_secondary_market -%}
  {%- comment -%} Secondary market: serve the native translated title untouched, unless the theme already emits its own. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless booster_config.theme_has_native_title -%}<title>{{ page_title | escape_once }}</title>{%- endunless -%}
{%- elsif booster_title != blank -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[title]", booster_item.title -%}
  {%- if baType == 'product' -%}
    {%- assign formatted_price = product.variants[0].price | money -%}
    {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[price]", formatted_price -%}
    {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[product_vendor]", booster_item.vendor -%}
    {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[product_type]", booster_item.type -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[content]", booster_item.content | strip_html -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[description]", booster_item.description -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace : "[shop_name]", shop.name -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace: "[author]", booster_item.author -%}
  {%- assign booster_title = booster_title | replace : "[shopify_seo_title]", page_title -%}
  <title>{{ booster_title | escape_once }}</title>
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%} No Booster-managed title (meta off): emit the default page_title only when the theme is not already outputting its own, else we duplicate it. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless booster_config.theme_has_native_title -%}
  <title>{{ page_title -}}
  {%- if current_tags -%} –
  {%- assign meta_tags = current_tags | join: ', ' -%}
  {%- assign translated_tags = 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: meta_tags -%}
  {%- if translated_tags contains 'translation missing' -%} {{ meta_tags}}{%- else -%} {{ translated_tags }}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if current_page != 1 -%} –
  {%- assign translated_page = 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page -%}
  {%- if translated_page contains 'translation missing' or translated_page contains 'I18n Error' -%} {{ current_page }}{%- else -%} {{ translated_page }}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  </title>
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}booster:title:end{%- endcomment -%}

{%- unless booster_config.google_verification_meta_tag == blank -%}
  {%- if booster_config.google_verification_meta_tag contains '<meta' -%}
